            {
                "entry_id": "f2a076ab-9103-314c-bf08-4cf98ea02d9d",
                "word": "doggerel",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5fcff4d0-fdfc-4a7c-ab5f-2342f4c8ff6a",
                        "entry_id": "f2a076ab-9103-314c-bf08-4cf98ea02d9d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "doggerels"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f22e5782-a30c-3a01-86a8-00d562264b45",
                        "entry_id": "f2a076ab-9103-314c-bf08-4cf98ea02d9d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A comic or humorous verse, usually irregular in measure."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0181256e-2410-43ce-931a-82f4db82dcf1",
                                "sense_id": "f22e5782-a30c-3a01-86a8-00d562264b45",
                                "text": "Taffy drew a long breath into his manly bosom, and kept it there as he read this characteristic French doggerel (for so he chose to call this touching little symphony in ère and ra)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ca99264-c97f-473c-a159-8e0ad91801c5",
                                "sense_id": "f22e5782-a30c-3a01-86a8-00d562264b45",
                                "text": "As he marched he sang a bit of doggerel in a high and quavering voice: / \"Sing a song 'a vic'try, / A pocketful 'a bullets, / Five an' twenty dead men / Baked in a—pie.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e7fbdc0-19dd-3401-a0df-9258e70a9097",
                        "entry_id": "f2a076ab-9103-314c-bf08-4cf98ea02d9d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any writing of crude composition."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e1da1cd-5414-4536-8f7c-25658b002b2e",
                                "sense_id": "8e7fbdc0-19dd-3401-a0df-9258e70a9097",
                                "text": "It is very rare to find good, personal analysis of events that does not degenerate into chest-beating, pettiness, pomposity, or political doggeral ^([sic])."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c0cb750-c185-47ab-99f7-bb4525c322ba",
                        "source_entry_id": "f2a076ab-9103-314c-bf08-4cf98ea02d9d",
                        "source_sense_description": "comic or humorous verse",
                        "target_lang_word": "ulevellenrijm",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e7f0576a-8124-4f1b-bb23-dc5bf2a1ef91",
                        "source_entry_id": "f2a076ab-9103-314c-bf08-4cf98ea02d9d",
                        "source_sense_description": "comic or humorous verse",
                        "target_lang_word": "vers de mirliton",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vers de mirliton",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "476c856c-8019-384d-a5cf-202dc9e3db4c",
                                        "entry_id": "31da26a5-f217-35d4-84e0-92bf59eaf7a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vers de faible qualité."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66a78001-eb9f-45d0-bb9e-5499ea70a4ae",
                                                "sense_id": "476c856c-8019-384d-a5cf-202dc9e3db4c",
                                                "text": "Loti répète au sujet d’Aicard, qu’il croit son ami : « C’est un sentimental. » Or je sais, et pertinemment, qu’il n’y eut jamais plus sec et dur, en son privé, que ce tourneur de vers de mirliton."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8114eb9f-b197-41ca-b3fd-04080c889e20",
                                                "sense_id": "476c856c-8019-384d-a5cf-202dc9e3db4c",
                                                "text": "Naulleau, en bon critique hautain, maladroit, vicieux, inique et de mauvaise foi qu'il est, rentre direct dans le chou de Francis en lui récitant la moitié d'un ver et en déduisant de cet octosyllabe tronqué que Francis fait des vers de mirliton !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
